statement:
Let $S, T \subseteq [n]$, and for a profile $p \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathrm{Fin}\,6$ write $x(p)$ for its $bc$-vote vector and $y(p)$ for its $ca$-vote vector, each lying in $\{0,1\}^n$. Averaging the product of Walsh characters over all $6^n$ profiles gives
\[
  \left(\tfrac{1}{6}\right)^{n} \sum_{p} \chi_S\bigl(x(p)\bigr)\,\chi_T\bigl(y(p)\bigr)
  \;=\;
  \begin{cases} \left(-\tfrac{1}{3}\right)^{\abs{S}} & \text{if } S = T,\\[2pt] 0 & \text{if } S \ne T. \end{cases}
\]

replaced:
Specialization of the general kernel to the $bc$--$ca$ vote pair: for all
$S,T\subseteq[n]$,
\[
  \Bigl(\tfrac16\Bigr)^{\!n}\sum_{p}
    \chi_S(\mathrm{bcVotes}(p))\,\chi_T(\mathrm{caVotes}(p))
  \;=\;
  \begin{cases} (-1/3)^{|S|} & S = T \\ 0 & S\ne T. \end{cases}
\]
